Yes, please.

On Fri, Oct 16, 2026 at 3:55=E2=80=AFPM Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com> wrote:

> Hi! After a request from and discussions with the authors of
> draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids [1], the chairs would like to determine
> whether there is consensus to request an early code point assignment; see
> [2] about the early allocation process. The code point in question is for
> 'trust_anchors' in the TLS ExtensionType Values registry, see Section 12.=
1
> of the I-D. As noted in [3], implementers have been using a value chosen =
at
> random and it has been stable since the initial draft. Please let the lis=
t
> know by 30 October 2023 if you support this early allocation.
>
> NOTE: A new registry is defined in Section 12.3 of the I-D, but we cannot
> ask for early creation of a registry.
>
> Cheers,
> spt (for the chairs)
>
> [1] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/
> [2] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc7120/
> [3] https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/tls/vD37D986i5YtFFvfLfkcte_WSxk=
/
> _______________________________________________
> TLS mailing list -- tls@ietf.org
> To unsubscribe send an email to tls-leave@ietf.org
>

--0000000000005a3b57065df603ad
